# Temporary media-worker AI waiver — reviewed 2026-07-20.
#
# Context:
# - The release gate still builds and imports the real AI runtime.
# - The product E2E gate exercises the full pipeline with AI enabled.
# - MediaPipe 0.10.18 requires protobuf < 5, while the fixed protobuf versions
#   reported by Trivy start at 5.29.6. Newer MediaPipe wheels removed the
#   solutions API used by the face/hand detector and do not ship Linux arm64.
#
# Compensating controls:
# - Protobuf is used internally by MediaPipe with bundled model assets; the
#   media-worker API does not accept or deserialize user-supplied protobuf data.
#
# Remove this waiver when MediaPipe offers a compatible fixed dependency graph.
CVE-2026-0994

# Temporary media-worker AI waiver — reviewed 2026-09-06.
#
# Context:
# - lightning (pytorch-lightning) 2.6.5 is RCE-able via
#   LightningModule.load_from_checkpoint on a malicious checkpoint file
#   (arbitrary module import from checkpoint _instantiator hyperparameters).
# - No fixed release exists yet: 2.6.5 is the latest PyPI release; the fix
#   is an unreleased upstream commit (no tagged version available to pin).
# - pyannote-audio==3.3.2 (used for whisperx diarization) requires
#   lightning>=2.0.1 and pulls this version transitively.
#
# Compensating controls:
# - The media-worker never calls load_from_checkpoint on user-supplied
#   input. Diarization loads only pyannote's pretrained pipeline from a
#   fixed, developer-configured HuggingFace model ID (gated by HF_TOKEN);
#   end users only ever supply video/audio media, never .ckpt files.
#
# Remove this waiver once a lightning/pytorch-lightning release ships the fix.
CVE-2026-58659
